After a month layoff I've come back to NAO for the June tournament.
The first alphabetically of the six classes I had remaining to ascend
was Archeologist; as this was my favorite role when I first started
playing NH in '93 and I had also ascended a dwarf Arc offline not long
ago, that seemed like a good place to start.

My first two dwarves met early deaths, and the third suffered YASD to
Demogorgon in the Valley of the Dead of all places. (Note to self:
Battling the toughest monster in the game while casually chatting with
boyfriend in IM is ill-advised.)  Fortunately, the winning game had
multiple bones piles, granting such goodies as a cloak of magic
resistance and bag of holding, and an early altar. Tried for
Grayswandir but ended up settling for Excalibur, which +7 and coupled
with +6 silver saber did just fine thank you. Silver dragon dropped
scales on Ludios; first time I haven't had to wish for SDSM in quite
some time (I used found shield of reflection up till then, but wanted
a free hand for spellcasting). Had a pet air elemental and dust vortex
for awhile; changed one into a green dragon via polytrap and kept him
for a good long time. Tamed a couple of purple worms late game; sadly,
couldn't get the survivor, Magenta, to follow me to Astral.

By the time I got the castle wand (0:3!), I had almost decided to play
wishless, but hadn't been able to find or poly up speed boots. So I
used one of the two magic lamps I'd discovered for charging scrolls
(also not found yet), got the speed boots, and used only one more wish
for a ring of teleport control just for getting out of Gehennom
faster. I did find a charging scroll eventually, so with the magic
markers I'd also obtained I probably could have played wishless after
all (if willing to give up speed boots) - oh well!

I wanted to play polyselfless but got lycanthropy; this and pre-MR
poly traps are usually the only way I'll break that conduct. I did
manage genocideless, as is usual when I play dwarves (to avoid YASD
via blessed-gen-h). Got magic missile spellbook to take care of those
flayers and disenchanters I usually geno. Liches were pretty annoying
with their summoning, but I managed. No close calls with sea monsters
except briefly on the Plane of Water; was glad to have saved and
charged up several wands of teleportation.

Rodney appeared only his two guaranteed times. Orb of Detection found
the portals. Second visited altar in Astral was the right one; avoided
Pestilence completely (though I was well-prepared with several full
healing potions, amulets of life saving, and cure sickness memorized
at 0% failure rate). Offered and ascended with my eighth NAO class and
finally got my ascension ration over 10%.

